1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,929
Open Audit log in the installed extension.

2
00:00:02,929 --> 00:00:06,786
This list shows records written during a real test run.

3
00:00:06,786 --> 00:00:11,000
You can see when a script ran and which agent requested it.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,824
Enter Export a sample order as the script name and orders-qa as the agent.

5
00:00:16,824 --> 00:00:18,180
Apply the filters.

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:22,250
You can also set a time range to narrow the search.

7
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:23,819
Open the verified row.

8
00:00:23,819 --> 00:00:28,599
The same run ID connects the queued event to the verified result.

9
00:00:28,599 --> 00:00:34,500
In this test we also checked the order number and quantity in the exported CSV.

10
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,641
Searching for a different agent returns an empty list.

11
00:00:38,641 --> 00:00:41,688
Reset the filters to see the runs again.

12
00:00:41,688 --> 00:00:47,000
An AI client can query these same records by time, script and agent.
